<title>USA: ATHLETICS-ENGLISH RUNNERS EVANS, SUTTON WIN AT CHICAGO MARATHON.</title>
<headline>ATHLETICS-ENGLISH RUNNERS EVANS, SUTTON WIN AT CHICAGO MARATHON.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1996-10-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Leading results from the</p>
<p>Chicago Marathon on Sunday, in which Briton Paul Evans won the</p>
<p>men's competition and compatriot Marian Sutton won the women's</p>
<p>race:</p>
<p>Men</p>
<p>1. Paul Evans (Britain)  two hours eight minutes 52 seconds</p>
<p>  2. Jerry Lawson (U.S.)		2:10:04</p>
<p>  3. Leonid Shvetsov (Russia)	 2:10:23</p>
<p>  4. Eamonn Martin (Britain)	  2:11:21</p>
<p>  5. Gary Staines (Britain)	   2:11:24</p>
<p>  6. Jackson Kabiga (Kenya)	   2:11:43</p>
<p>  7. Carlos Bautista (Mexico)	 2:12:17</p>
<p>  8. Luis Reyes (Mexico)		2:13:04</p>
<p>  9. Ole Hjelle (Norway)		2:13:19</p>
<p> 10. Antonio Rodrigues (Portugal)   2:13:27</p>
<p>Women</p>
<p>  1. Marian Sutton (Britain)	  2:30:41</p>
<p>  2. Kristy Johnson (U.S.)	    2:31:06</p>
<p>  3. Danuta Bartozek (Canada)	 2:33:01</p>
<p>  4. Gitte Karlshoj (Denmark)	 2:33:53</p>
<p>  5. Irina Bogacheva (Russia)	 2:34:36</p>
<p>  6. Bonnie McReynolds (U.S.)	 2:39:18</p>
<p>  7. Debbie Kilpatrick (U.S.)	 2:39:23</p>
<p>  8. Paivi Tikkanen (Finland)	 2:39:36</p>
<p>  9. Ritva Lemettinen (Finland)     2:42:00</p>
<p> 10. Sharon Stubler (U.S.)	    2:42:39</p>
</text>
